{
  "_readme": [
    "Delta compatibility fixtures for quill-table-better 1.2.3.",
    "",
    "Recorded by `dart run tool/gen_goldens.dart --suite table-better` against the",
    "real plugin bundle running on quill 2.0.3, and replayed against the port by",
    "test/unit/table_better/goldens_test.dart.",
    "",
    "Cell and row ids are random by construction in BOTH implementations",
    "(`cellId()` / `tableId()`), so the comparison canonicalises them: the first",
    "id seen becomes id#1, the second id#2, and so on, on each side. Structure",
    "and the association between cells and rows are preserved by that mapping —",
    "two cells sharing a row still share one afterwards — so nothing meaningful",
    "is smoothed over.",
    "",
    "setup: {\"delta\": ops} or {\"html\": \"...\"}. actions: entries of the form",
    "{\"module\": \"method\", \"args\": [...]} call the table-better module, and",
    "{\"method\": ..., \"args\": [...]} call the Quill API."
  ],
